+# the interface MTU: at upstream's 296 byte default the TCP MSS comes out at
+# 256, so every segment spends 44 bytes of header on 212 of payload.
+#
+# Raising it to 1500 does fix that framing overhead and roughly doubles the
+# audio the link carries, but this board's PPP link does not survive it: the
+# interface stops answering LCP echo after about 30 s of audio, and after
+# about 6 minutes even with no audio at all. That was measured, not guessed --
+# see the soak and idle-control scripts in ~/. Back at 296 the same link runs
